{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghyQ8JwvwWC2hbY4yN4q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UEJQVJBQxrTodcEjJk7fuL","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/56-about.js'; s=open(p).read()\nT=[\"About 14 real issues across headless suites, the autopilot calibration runs, the browser checks and screenshots (plus 5 bugs in the tests themselves).\",\n\"6 were game-breaking: a run's stop index started one ahead (the train never left the first station), a field name that shadowed a method (a crash every step), a setting applied before game.settings existed (a crash at boot), deep links racing the async boot (a crash in the browser), the tutorial never ending, and the S2 freight joining into an occupied block so the player passed a red signal.\",\n\"The autopilot playthrough: the skill-1 autopilot driving every stage and asserting PERFECT stops, every event fired and rank S. It found the stop-index bug, the freight bug, the tutorial bug and the timetable calibration problems, and it is how the timetables were fitted.\",\n\"The gallery test that draws all 13 rail shots into a stub canvas: it only proves nothing throws; the screenshots of the same shots were what actually judged the look.\"]\nEN=[\"Headless determinism: game.advance with exact 1/120 s steps made a full scripted career (and timetable calibration) run in Node, and the standard Shell gave pause, settings, rebinding and full screen for free.\",\n\"Yes: game.start with boot steps starts the first scene asynchronously, so deep-link game.go() calls right after start failed in the browser; and in a custom E.View a Humanoid facing +PI/2 faces the camera, which I guessed backwards at first.\",\n\"The rail renderer (rail.js): a fork of road.js with several diverging tracks, strips (extrusions) for platforms, trains, buildings and tunnels, a rear-facing camera and square pixels. The train physics, signalling and the predictive autopilot came next.\",\n\"Fitting a full dashboard (timetable, speedometer, notch strip, lamps, buttons, the master controller) into 320 to 427 pixels of width while keeping the 5x7 font as the minimum for a TV at 10 feet.\",\n\"Seven patches: the new rail.js module; a Dialog voice function hook (per-letter Babble syllables); a group filter for the Shell settings screen (live Dev sliders, hidden from normal Settings); the PlayStation glyph default and the four PlayStation symbols in the 5x7 font; audio.bus() and noiseBuffer() so custom synth nodes follow the volume settings; bow, point and flag poses; ignoring Options while Create is held in a hub session.\",\n\"Generalise road.js into a pseudo-3D extrusion renderer (several lanes or tracks, side objects as extruded strips, a reverse camera, square pixels), so first-person vehicle games on rails, roads or rivers start from more than a single road.\"]\nPR=[\"The concrete deliverables and checks: a named file, an exact exit-interview shape, a 10-foot controller-first UX brief, and an AI Hub harness that gives a hard pass or fail. The plan's numbers (physics check values, judgment windows) made tuning testable.\",\n\"Usage asks for API cost, tokens and session time, which an agent inside the session cannot see; and the plan was written for another run's timestamp and model tag, so the file names had to be translated.\",\n\"Scope: a full career of six stages, the duel, the hub round, attract, Dev Mode and all-procedural audio in one session; and calibrating timetables so the AI driver arrives on the second.\",\n\"Say which features matter most if time runs short (the plan's cut order helped), and give the agent its usage numbers or drop that field.\"]\ns=s.replace(\"  testing: [\\n    'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown'\\n  ],\",\"  testing: \"+repr(T).replace(\"\\\\'\",\"'\").replace(\"[\\\"\",\"[\\n    \\\"\").replace(\"\\\"]\",\"\\\"\\n  ]\")+\",\")\ns=s.replace(\"  engine: [\\n    'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown'\\n  ],\",\"  engine: \"+repr(EN)+\",\")\ns=s.replace(\"  prompt: [\\n    'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown'\\n  ]\",\"  prompt: \"+repr(PR))\ns=s.replace(\"usage: 'unknown'\",\"usage: 'unknown (no cost or token figures are visible inside the session; wall time about 1 h 45 min)'\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nimport json\nsrc=open(p).read()\nEOF\nnode -e \"\nglobal.window={};global.My3D2dge={version:'0.85.2'};eval(require('fs').readFileSync('src/56-about.js','utf8'));const A=window.DH.ABOUT;console.log(A.testing.length,A.engine.length,A.prompt.length,A.source.usage)\"","description":"Fill feedback in About data"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1278,"cache_read_input_tokens":612753,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1278},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2971b458-25be-4a87-89a5-fd55d735f2d2","uuid":"49e9f23f-bd29-4ecb-b3e5-ebd6277c2c61","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:33:33.872Z","request_id":"req_011CghyQ7wNHDjf1pJ8tAfo6","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01UEJQVJBQxrTodcEjJk7fuL":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/56-about.js'; s=open(p).read()\nT=[\"About 14 real issues across headless suites, the autopilot calibration runs, the browser checks and screenshots (plus 5 bugs in the tests themselves).\",\n\"6 were game-breaking: a run's stop index started one ahead (the train never left the first station), a field name that shadowed a method (a crash every step), a setting applied before game.settings existed (a crash at boot), deep links racing the async boot (a crash in the browser), the tutorial never ending, and the S2 freight joining into an occupied block so the player passed a red signal.\",\n\"The autopilot playthrough: the skill-1 autopilot driving every stage and asserting PERFECT stops, every event fired and rank S. It found the stop-index bug, the freight bug, the tutorial bug and the timetable calibration problems, and it is how the timetables were fitted.\",\n\"The gallery test that draws all 13 rail shots into a stub canvas: it only proves nothing throws; the screenshots of the same shots were what actually judged the look.\"]\nEN=[\"Headless determinism: game.advance with exact 1/120 s steps made a full scripted career (and timetable calibration) run in Node, and the standard Shell gave pause, settings, rebinding and full screen for free.\",\n\"Yes: game.start with boot steps starts the first scene asynchronously, so deep-link game.go() calls right after start failed in the browser; and in a custom E.View a Humanoid facing +PI/2 faces the camera, which I guessed backwards at first.\",\n\"The rail renderer (rail.js): a fork of road.js with several diverging tracks, strips (extrusions) for platforms, trains, buildings and tunnels, a rear-facing camera and square pixels. The train physics, signalling and the predictive autopilot came next.\",\n\"Fitting a full dashboard (timetable, speedometer, notch strip, lamps, buttons, the master controller) into 320 to 427 pixels of width while keeping the 5x7 font as the minimum for a TV at 10 feet.\",\n\"Seven patches: the new rail.js module; a Dialog voice function hook (per-letter Babble syllables); a group filter for the Shell settings screen (live Dev sliders, hidden from normal Settings); the PlayStation glyph default and the four PlayStation symbols in the 5x7 font; audio.bus() and noiseBuffer() so custom synth nodes follow the volume settings; bow, point and flag poses; ignoring Options while Create is held in a hub session.\",\n\"Generalise road.js into a pseudo-3D extrusion renderer (several lanes or tracks, side objects as extruded strips, a reverse camera, square pixels), so first-person vehicle games on rails, roads or rivers start from more than a single road.\"]\nPR=[\"The concrete deliverables and checks: a named file, an exact exit-interview shape, a 10-foot controller-first UX brief, and an AI Hub harness that gives a hard pass or fail. The plan's numbers (physics check values, judgment windows) made tuning testable.\",\n\"Usage asks for API cost, tokens and session time, which an agent inside the session cannot see; and the plan was written for another run's timestamp and model tag, so the file names had to be translated.\",\n\"Scope: a full career of six stages, the duel, the hub round, attract, Dev Mode and all-procedural audio in one session; and calibrating timetables so the AI driver arrives on the second.\",\n\"Say which features matter most if time runs short (the plan's cut order helped), and give the agent its usage numbers or drop that field.\"]\ns=s.replace(\"  testing: [\\n    'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown'\\n  ],\",\"  testing: \"+repr(T).replace(\"\\\\'\",\"'\").replace(\"[\\\"\",\"[\\n    \\\"\").replace(\"\\\"]\",\"\\\"\\n  ]\")+\",\")\ns=s.replace(\"  engine: [\\n    'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown'\\n  ],\",\"  engine: \"+repr(EN)+\",\")\ns=s.replace(\"  prompt: [\\n    'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown'\\n  ]\",\"  prompt: \"+repr(PR))\ns=s.replace(\"usage: 'unknown'\",\"usage: 'unknown (no cost or token figures are visible inside the session; wall time about 1 h 45 min)'\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nimport json\nsrc=open(p).read()\nEOF\nnode -e \"\nglobal.window={};global.My3D2dge={version:'0.85.2'};eval(require('fs').readFileSync('src/56-about.js','utf8'));const A=window.DH.ABOUT;console.log(A.testing.length,A.engine.length,A.prompt.length,A.source.usage)\"","description":"Fill feedback in About data"}}}
